<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Bafana buys Samrand for 105 mln rand.</title>
<headline>S.African Bafana buys Samrand for 105 mln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bafana Holdings Ltd said on Monday that it had bought control of Samrand Development Holdings from Malaysia's Landmarks Berhad for 57.58 million Malaysian ringitt, equivalent to 104.86 million rand.</p>
<p>The deal, secured by buying Samrand's controlling shareholder LB International Ltd (LBI), valued each Samrand share at 108.1 cents.</p>
<p>Bafana, an investment vehicle for Malaysian owned New Republic Bank, said it would make a standby offer to all Samrand minority shareholders at 108.1 cents a share. The LBI deal means Bafana has 88 percent of Samrand.</p>
<p>New Republic's chairman Dato'Samsudin Abu Hassan is now also to be chairman of Samrand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
